From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 49/55] mux: refuse a terminal over a connection that uses the
 none cipher

The none switch is only made when the session has no terminal, because what
is typed would go over the network in clear text. A control master started with
NoneSwitch yes and -N has no terminal, so it switches, and a later session
shared over it with -t or -tt got a terminal on the none cipher.

Refuse a terminal request in mux_master_process_new_session() while the
connection uses the none cipher. The client then makes a connection of its own,
which is encrypted.
---
 mux.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mux.c b/mux.c
index c9157a597..a37571f18 100644
--- a/mux.c
+++ b/mux.c
@@ -476,6 +476,18 @@ mux_master_process_new_session(struct ssh *ssh, u_int rid,
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The none cipher is only switched to when the session has no terminal,
+	 * since what is typed would go in clear. A session shared over this
+	 * connection is no different, so refuse a terminal on it.
+	 */
+	if (cctx->want_tty && ssh->none) {
+		debug2_f("terminal refused: the connection uses the none cipher");
+		reply_error(reply, MUX_S_PERMISSION_DENIED, rid,
+		    "A terminal is not allowed on a connection that uses the none cipher");
+		goto cleanup;
+	}
+
 	/* Try to pick up ttymodes from client before it goes raw */
 	if (cctx->want_tty && tcgetattr(new_fd[0], &cctx->tio) == -1)
 		error_f("tcgetattr: %s", strerror(errno));
-- 
